    "explanation": "Rider, you are refunded the whole contested SGD 6.00 cancellation fee. Driver, no compensation is payable to you, and the trip is referred for a false-arrival record.\n\nA no-show fee is chargeable only if all four conditions in POL-NS-01 hold, and three of them fail here. (a) holds: the trip record does contain an 'arrived' event at 16:14:40. (b) fails: the GPS trace's 79 driver fixes never come nearer than 881.64 m to the T4 pickup pin (mean 951.64 m, maximum 1,467.21 m) against the 150 m arrival radius the fee schedule sets for the AIRPORT zone class, and the derived arrival block records 0 qualifying in-radius fixes. (c) fails: the longest continuous in-geofence run is 0.0 seconds against the 480-second AIRPORT minimum. (d) fails: the trip was terminated by the rider at 16:23:40 with reason code RIDER_CHANGED_MIND, which is not one of the three codes limb (d) recognises, and no boarding event is recorded.\n\nBecause the driver was more than 300 m from the pin at the 16:14:40 'arrived' timestamp, that marker is FALSE under POL-NS-05. Recomputing the waiting clock from the first qualifying in-geofence fix, there is no qualifying in-geofence fix anywhere in the trip, so POL-NS-05(ii) applies: the SGD 6.00 is refunded in full, no driver compensation is payable, and a false-arrival record is directed in the referrals list. The driver's explanation that he pressed 'arrived' so the rider would know he was near does not change this — the marker is tested against the trace, not against intent. His account of waiting in the holding area does not engage POL-NS-03 either: that clause reaches only a driver stationary outside the arrival radius but within 400 m of the pin, and the trace places him between 881.64 m and 1,467.21 m throughout. The chat log is consistent with that: asked at 16:15:40 'where are you? I'm at the T4 pickup door', the driver answered 'not yet' at 16:16:20, a minute and forty seconds after marking arrival.\n\nThe rider's separate assertion that the driver 'wanted a surcharge and thought I was a tourist' is not supported by the record: the chat log is complete and unredacted at three messages, matching the trip record's chat_message_count of 3, and the driver's only substantive line — 'if wait too long app charge you not me' — states the platform's own wait rule. That element of the claim is set aside; it carries nothing.\n\nNeither rider-contact exoneration nor escalation is engaged. POL-NS-04 does not apply because the driver replied within 120 seconds (rider 16:15:40, driver 16:16:20), a point both sides accepted. The POL-NS-07 anti-farming check does not trip: 2 no-show terminations in 30 days against 95 completed trips is a ratio of 0.021, below the 0.08 gate, and both limbs are required. No POL-NS-08 limb is breached — the arrived timestamp falls on the 10-second fix cadence, the trace has no gaps and 79 fixes, the chat log is complete, and the fee reconciles — so the apparent conflict between the trip record's arrival event and the trace is resolved by POL-NS-05 and nothing escalates.\n\nThe money figures: the fare breakdown records a SGD 6.00 cancellation fee, SGD 0.00 of it already refunded. The resolution rule takes the greater of the AIRPORT zone-class fee (SGD 6.00) and the RYDE_X vehicle-tier fee (SGD 4.00), which is SGD 6.00 and matches the ledger, so there is no amount defect. The refund is the SGD 6.00 cancellation-fee line.\n\nThe GPS trace, trip record, chat log and fare breakdown each carry weight 1.0, and the deciding facts — that the driver never entered the arrival geofence and never began the required hold — rest on them, so confidence is not discounted. The only below-weight artifact in the bundle is EV-ADVIS-00614-01 at weight 0.0, which is MISSING and carries no fact: it makes POL-NS-06(i) dwell accumulation unavailable, but there are no in-geofence intervals to accumulate, so it does not affect the outcome."
